#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Gapmer ASO Design, allele-selective: INDELS AS WELL AS SNPs, and what a compound spells out.

  - An allele-selective run now rebuilds the target with the track's indels APPLIED, so an ASO can be
    designed across a deletion's join or over inserted bases -- neither of which exists in the reference.
    Indels used to be excluded from the design, so the strategy quietly tiled around substitutions only.
  - A candidate must cover the whole feature, not merely touch it: every inserted base, or both bases
    either side of a deletion's join. Covering half an insertion does not discriminate the alleles.
  - A compound's sequence -- the label above it, and the per-base letters over it -- is the TARGET, the
    strand that lines up with the track underneath, unless the chemistry is already spelling out its own
    bases (11 px per residue), where those letters are the synthesis strand and the label carries the
    synthesis sequence instead.
  - A variant is matched against the track sequence in whichever way that track writes its alleles
    (reference/alternate or the complemented reference0/alternate0), instead of assuming one of them: on a
    minus-strand gene the other writing disagreed with the base under the variant and it was dropped. A
    variant that matches no writing is now reported, with what the track actually reads there, rather
    than silently skipped. An indel's anchor is tried one base either way, since whether a loader stores
    its position at the anchor or at the first changed base is a convention rather than a fact.

    sudo python3 install-allele-indels.py /opt/baja-apps

Needs install-allele-selective-tiling.py first. Edits track-design-menu.js, design-scope-from-workbench.js,
py/ssaso/design.py and flexigraph/oligo.js (each backed up as <file>.before-allele-indels). Refuses,
changing nothing, if a file differs. Safe to run twice.
"""
